```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center;
  align-items: center;
}
```

- Parent gets `display: flex`. The child needs nothing.
- `justify-content: center` handles the main axis (horizontal by default).
- `align-items: center` handles the cross axis (vertical).
- Parent needs a real height or nothing moves vertically. Use `min-height: 100vh` for full viewport, or an explicit hei...
